{"id":"071e0481-3650-4f7d-97f6-36ff4b1eb8d6","name":"Why MCP is Awesome","path":"WWW / Blog / Why MCP is Awesome","docTypeId":"9084a58d-99f2-4576-8b1a-b77f29725c81","templateId":"e0dd05d7-3b6b-413d-9277-084e95b5d1c0","state":"Published","domains":[],"values":[{"editorAlias":"Umbraco.TextBox","culture":null,"segment":null,"alias":"title","value":"Why MCP is Awesome"},{"editorAlias":"Umbraco.TextBox","culture":null,"segment":null,"alias":"date","value":"October 7, 2026"},{"editorAlias":"Umbraco.TextBox","culture":null,"segment":null,"alias":"excerpt","value":"MCP standardizes how AI models interact with external systems, making integration seamless and powerful."},{"editorAlias":"Umbraco.BlockGrid","culture":null,"segment":null,"alias":"body","value":{"layout":{"Umbraco.BlockGrid":[{"$type":"BlockGridLayoutItem","columnSpan":12,"rowSpan":1,"areas":[],"contentKey":"a7ce3dbf-8255-43e9-b5a1-a8b0fc18a43d","settingsKey":null},{"$type":"BlockGridLayoutItem","columnSpan":12,"rowSpan":1,"areas":[],"contentKey":"6ebbc882-e4b4-4031-99fc-7b3387dbfa3e","settingsKey":null},{"$type":"BlockGridLayoutItem","columnSpan":12,"rowSpan":1,"areas":[],"contentKey":"6f6235d4-d064-4d3f-813f-fc844e75b873","settingsKey":null},{"$type":"BlockGridLayoutItem","columnSpan":12,"rowSpan":1,"areas":[],"contentKey":"8de91183-c157-47a2-81e9-7e96206a35d2","settingsKey":null}]},"contentData":[{"contentTypeKey":"7903dd9f-d0c3-4726-96c0-35ae9ca775bf","key":"a7ce3dbf-8255-43e9-b5a1-a8b0fc18a43d","values":[{"editorAlias":"Umbraco.RichText","culture":null,"segment":null,"alias":"text","value":{"markup":"<p>Model Context Protocol (MCP) represents a paradigm shift in how AI systems interact with external tools and data. At its core, MCP provides a standardized interface that allows language models to seamlessly access external resources without proprietary integrations.</p>","blocks":{"layout":{},"contentData":[],"settingsData":[],"expose":[]}}}]},{"contentTypeKey":"eb00cb37-ae89-4b94-ac95-d7f6647832d0","key":"6